# Profile flows-schedule (feature 009, research R12, contracts/parity.md §1): two apps that share the clock of the
# scheduled flows (SYNCHRONIZATION_STORE=redis, own namespace), like the redis nodes of the Directus blackbox
# schedule-hook.test.ts. This pair shares the parity database and runs a flow every 2 s while the test is on, so only
# src/flows/schedule.test.ts brings it up (profileUp) and stops it (profileStop); never list it in
# `env-up --profiles`. Own bus, lock and cache namespaces so the main pair never loads or runs its flows through them.
# FLOWS_SCHEDULE_HOOK_NAME is set per container in docker-compose.yml. Test values only.
CACHE_NAMESPACE=parity-flows-schedule
REDIS_BUS_NAMESPACE=parity-flows-schedule:bus
REDIS_LOCK_NAMESPACE=parity-flows-schedule:lock
SYNCHRONIZATION_STORE=redis
SYNCHRONIZATION_NAMESPACE=parity-flows-schedule:sync
FLOWS_ENV_ALLOW_LIST=FLOWS_SCHEDULE_HOOK_NAME
LOG_LEVEL=info
